  "2026-10-30T23:52:22.479Z",codex-agent,"Resumed delivery: reviewed retained README and generated window artifacts; rejected only temporary-fixture merge attributes. Next merge current main, preserve append-only tracker history, prove all three acceptance criteria with behavioral reverts, validate a public tracker copy, and run npm/Bun release gates with two workers."
  "2026-10-30T23:55:06.544Z",codex-agent,"Merged current main source and toolchain (SDK 2026.10.27), retaining all new progress/variance commands. Window reads request native event-chain verification. Public-data read-only validation at main 57cc37a: 109 items, 1099 mutation events, 110 streams, 2 pages, 224 authoritative files unchanged; 14663-byte JSON packet, identical restart, complete preview. Added reproducible validation entry and six-host packed window acceptance."
  "2026-10-30T23:58:21.627Z",codex-agent,"Verified four behavioral mutants in a disposable copy: advancing during preview breaks restart equality; timestamp-only membership drops the late event; disabling history regression certification reports lost streams complete; bypassing cursor coverage certification reports a damaged boundary complete. Each selected mutant exits 1; restored implementation passes all four selected regressions. Also fixed cursorless terminal pages, certification of more than ten deleted streams, and packet output contention. Stdout-only calls now preview because host rendering occurs after handler return; admission requires atomic file delivery under the cursor lease."
  "2026-10-31T00:01:38.049Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm linked-test execution passed 33 tests: 521 seeded operations, 27 windows, 458 SDK events partitioned exactly. Disposable behavioral reverts each failed as expected; restored four-case selection passed 4/4. Delivery-before-retention failure recovery and peer interleaving are covered. Running complete npm then Bun release checks serially with isolated git identity and two test workers."
  "2026-10-31T00:16:30.233Z",codex-agent,"Full-gate integration exposed host TOON sparsity (nulls and empty arrays omitted) and generic every-command fixtures missing the new required cursor option. Fixed acceptance to compare TOON against the host-produced lean JSON, and adapted SDK/installed materialization probes (3/3 passing). Focused window coverage now measures 100% lines/statements/branches/functions across 33 tests; every threshold remains unchanged. Serialization also preserves reserved object keys. Public docs now distinguish the native cursor chain from per-stream progress in late-only windows."
  "2026-10-31T00:27:40.620Z",codex-agent,"Fresh Node packed acceptance passed all six scenarios: npm/bun project-local current 2026.10.27 and minimum 2026.10.20 plus npm/bun global current hosts. Every receipt verifies windows, progress, variance, native materialization and reconciled fixture counts (four 2-item cases, two 1-item cases). Current npm/Bun full release gates are running serially; the existing packed-timing issue remains the separate timeout reference. Rechecked overlap after merging main: per-item progress cursors and selected-revision commitment variance do not provide retained multi-item reporting windows."
  "2026-10-31T00:37:07.812Z",codex-agent,"Final concurrency correction routes admission, preview and empty-window file delivery through one SDK fenced lease and boundary CAS. The empty/preview peer-output regression fails when that path is bypassed. All five behavioral mutants exit 1; restored selection passes 5/5. Focused final source passes 35 tests and 100% lines/statements/branches/functions. SDK inspection confirms 2026.10.20 lacks acquireLockLease; package peer and manifest floors now require the already-pinned 2026.10.27, with no development dependency bump. This is needed for generation fencing and verified event reads."
  "2026-10-31T00:58:58.018Z",codex-agent,"Complete isolated npm release check on current source: 348/350 tests passed; only the two instrumented packed matrices exceeded the unchanged 290000 ms limit. All runtime modules, including reporting-window.ts, measured 100% lines/statements/branches/functions. The unfinished acceptance-script paths leave all-authored-source totals at 96.17% lines/statements, 99.88% branches, 97.59% functions, so the npm gate correctly failed. Bun full gate is now running. Timing follow-up: pm-slack-standup-packed-timing."
  "2026-10-31T01:23:30.243Z",codex-agent,"Complete isolated Bun release check matches npm: 348/350 tests passed, with only both 290000 ms instrumented packed-matrix timeouts. All runtime modules measured 100% in every dimension; overall authored-source coverage remains 96.17% lines/statements, 99.88% branches and 97.59% functions because acceptance-script runs were interrupted. Both gates correctly fail unchanged thresholds. Final-source standalone Node and Bun fresh-pack matrices are running next; exact-head CI remains required."
  "2026-10-31T01:48:41.064Z",codex-agent,"Final-source behavioral revert receipts (disposable non-git copies): runStandupWindowCommand with preview protection disabled fails restart packet equality (exit 1); eventInStandupWindow with offset fallback disabled fails the exactly-once late-append regression (exit 1); standupWindowCoverageRegressions returning no regressions fails missing-history incompleteness (exit 1); standupWindowHasCursorCoverage always returning true fails damaged-cursor incompleteness (exit 1); empty/preview output outside the shared lease fails preservation of peer output (exit 1). Restored implementation passes all five selected cases (exit 0). Full source includes 35 focused window/model cases; the seeded model partitions 458 SDK events across 27 windows after 521 operations."
  "2026-10-31T01:48:42.211Z",codex-agent,"Final-source fresh-pack acceptance passed 6/6 scenarios under Node and 6/6 under Bun. Both tarballs are identical: SHA-256 c3d3fd0cde498bfa1e7372a6f5620c82b899e64b7d6445c75d48e430000721d3, 129382 bytes, 45 entries, all four window artifacts, host floor 2026.10.27. Five installed-CLI probes passed (cap, three invalid limits, explicit file-output preview). Canonical-reader 1/1, production audit 0 vulnerabilities, pack inventory, changelog, release-date and publish-attestation checks passed. Public tracker final validation reproduced 109 items, 1099 events, 110 streams, 2 pages, 14663 compact JSON bytes and 224 unchanged authoritative files. Complete local npm/Bun checks each remain 348/350 with the two unchanged 290-second timing failures; exact-head CI is pending."
  "2026-10-31T01:52:11.201Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/175 . Acceptance/revert table, final public-data numbers, local gate counts, host-floor rationale and immutable artifact receipt are in the PR and linked validation docs. All tracker writes are being completed before the final evidence push and exact-head CI verification. The local instrumented timing issue remains open; neither full local release gate is claimed passed. Claim is released for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress and is not closed."
  "2026-10-31T02:09:55.487Z",codex-agent,"Final-head Node 22 CI completed 349/350 tests: the inherited npm launcher packed matrix exceeded 290000 ms; the unset-launcher matrix passed. This is now a CI gate failure, so implementation work is reclaimed to reduce redundant install/coverage overhead while preserving every assertion, six installation scenarios, worker limit, timeout and coverage threshold. No review threads are being changed."
  "2026-10-31T02:18:45.989Z",codex-agent,"CI timing remediation changes only the acceptance driver and its environment contract test; shipped runtime files and the recorded tarball are unchanged. Focused driver tests pass 12/12; lint, types, zero-duplication and docstrings pass (140 documented declarations across the same 19 authored source files). Both claims are temporarily reclaimed while the failure is fixed; a fresh pushed head will receive complete CI verification."
  "2026-10-31T02:33:12.185Z",codex-agent,"CI timing fix verification: linked tests passed 35/35 window/model cases plus 12/12 driver contracts. Behavioral revert forwarding the canonical V8 counter directory into consumers fails; restored selection passes 1/1. Types, lint, duplication and docstrings pass; shipped runtime files, package metadata and tarball contents are unchanged. Claims are released before the replacement-head push; fresh CI remains required."
  "2026-10-31T03:11:56.600Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on 348fb0d, fixed by hand: (1) window sections no longer cap up_next at three; every touched open item is listed, and touched corpus items no section shows (canceled, declared requests) are named in window.unsectioned_items. New command test fails on revert (0/1). Pinned public replay at 57cc37a now accounts for all 109 touched items: 102 done + 5 up next + 2 canceled unsectioned; packet 15,036 bytes; restart identical; 224 files unchanged. (2) reporting-window-public.ts is pinned to the documented commit, with STANDUP_PUBLIC_COMMIT override. (3) The two chmod-based failure tests skip when running as root. (4) README documents that every run scans the full journal and fixes the split paragraph. reporting-window suites 36/36; typecheck, lint, docstring (140), duplication 0%, changelog:check pass."
  "2026-10-31T04:16:38.454Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on 670a543: doc focused-test count 34 -> 35 (historical 35/35 CI line unchanged). Declined the locale-independent position comparator: the pinned SDK's own compareHistoryEventPosition (node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/dist/core/history/event-index.js) orders by ts.localeCompare, stream_id.localeCompare, then offset; compareStandupWindowPositions mirrors it, and code-unit order would diverge from the SDK's event order."
  "2026-10-31T05:23:16.058Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on b22b66c: installedHostEnvironment now sets NODE_V8_COVERAGE to an own empty value instead of deleting it, because Node child_process copies the parent's NODE_V8_COVERAGE into a child env that lacks the key (copyProcessEnvToEnv). The new test 'installed host children never inherit the parent's counter directory' spawns a real child; with the old delete, the child received the parent's directory (fails on revert). Typecheck, lint, docstring (140) and duplication 0% pass; the full packed suite is left to CI because of host load."
  "2026-10-31T06:18:22.342Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on ceb888c (6 findings). Fixed: (1) scan cap trips only when the window exceeds maxEvents on any page; a non-final page reaching exactly the cap keeps reading already-covered pages. New test fails on revert (0/1); the old cap test now expects capping at 3 events on page 3. (2) README: one cursor file per consumer; the raw pm history events --since cursor is timestamp-ordered and skips backdated appends, so it does not replace standup window. Both validation links now use repository URLs, because validation docs are not shipped. (3) Packed acceptance is labeled historical for 415328b. (4) Packed acceptance now also runs --no-advance --output and asserts no admission. Declined: 'read the negated flag from advance'. The real installed CLI on hosts 2026.10.27 and 2026.10.28 does not admit with --no-advance --output (no cursor file, admitted:false); the control without the flag admits. Window suites 37/37; typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication 0%, changelog pass."
  "2026-10-31T07:18:06.847Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on 790dad6: (1) standupWindowCoverageRegressions returns no regressions for a capped scan, because streams on unread pages are unread, not regressed; the capped window is already incomplete via event_cap_exceeded. New test 'a capped scan reports no regressions…' fails on revert (0/1). (2) README and validation doc qualify the fencing guarantee: it holds with the built-in lock provider, while an extension lock_acquire override runs fence() unfenced (pinned SDK LockLease.fence doc) and must exclude or fence concurrent commits itself. Window suites 38/38; typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication 0% (after extracting twoPageJournal), changelog pass."
  "2026-10-31T08:23:03.776Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on fcfb656. (1) The scan counts events per stream; an uncapped scan whose stream offsets are not all read (a backdated append sorted before a page already read) reports gapStreams, and the window is incomplete with stream_offset_gap instead of admitting coverage it never read (which would make later runs report cursor_coverage_missing until repair). The reasons a scan establishes live in standupWindowScanIncompleteReasons, which is unit-tested on every branch. The pinned public replay at 57cc37a (1,099 events incl. history_redact/repair) has no gaps and stays complete, at 15,036 bytes. (2) README: one cursor file and one output file per consumer, because the lease is keyed by the cursor file; the losing-reporter guarantee applies to reporters sharing a cursor. Window suites 39/39; typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication 0%, changelog pass."
  "2026-10-31T09:24:40.439Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on 272aa63 (3 minor). (1) The corpus is read after the journal scan, so a mutation between them lands in a later window instead of being admitted with a stale row. New test: a peer closes the item right after the corpus read, and the close then appears in the next window with the item done. It fails with the old order (0/1). (2) writeError takes the command label; standup window --output failures now say 'standup window: could not write'. The delivery-failure test asserts the label and fails on revert (0/1). (3) README: stdout is TOON (JSON with --json), but the --output file is always pretty-printed JSON. Window suites 40/40 (units and runtime-export also pass, 133 total); typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication 0% (after extracting admittedInProgressItem), changelog pass."
  "2026-10-31T10:24:00.590Z",codex,"CodeRabbit round on d4a0784 (major, a regression from my reorder): with the scan now first, invalid history reached the SDK reader before the corpus's verified-history read and surfaced as a raw SDK error instead of history_unavailable. Fix: only the SDK page read is wrapped, so a history read or verification failure is ProgressRefusal('history_unavailable') (the package's single safe refusal), while the scan's own window_* refusals keep their codes; there is no conditional branch. New test: an appended malformed history line refuses the window with history_unavailable; it fails on revert (0/1). Window suites 41/41; typecheck, lint, docstring, duplication 0% and changelog pass."
